ith status Placed, a sequential order number ORD- followed by 6 zero-padded digits, each line&#39;s current part price as unit price, and total = subtotal + delivery charge.</li><li><b>REQ-21</b> If a place-order request has no lines, a quantity outside 1–99, an unknown part number, an address outside 5–200 characters, or a missing or unknown delivery option, then the orders API shall reject it with status 400 and save no order.</li><li><b>REQ-22</b> If any line&#39;s quantity is above the part&#39;s stock when an order is placed, then the orders API shall reject the order with status 409 and return each affected part number with the stock now available, saving no order.</li><li><b>REQ-23</b> When an order is placed successfully, the portal shall empty the cart and show the new order number.</li><li><b>REQ-24</b> If placing an order fails with a network error or a server error, then the portal shall show an error message, which for a network error tells the buyer to check My orders before retrying, and keep the cart lines, address and delivery option so the buyer can try again.</li><li><b>REQ-36</b> The portal shall show all three screens without horizontal scrolling at viewport widths from 360 px upwards.</li><li><b>REQ-37</b> The portal shall give every form field a visible text label and let the buyer reach and use every control by keyboard alone.</li><li><b>REQ-39</b> When the orders API rejects an order with a 409 stock conflict, the cart shall lower each affected line to the stock now available with the message &quot;Only n available&quot;, remove each affected line whose available stock is 0 with the message &quot;&lt;part name&gt; is now out of stock&quot;, and keep all other lines.</li><li><b>REQ-40</b> While a place-order request is in progress, the checkout shall disable &quot;Place order&quot;.</li><li><b>REQ-41</b> When the buyer opens the cart, the cart shall fetch the current price of each line&#39;s part from the parts API and use only those current prices for unit prices, line totals and totals.</li><li><b>REQ-42</b> If the current part data fetched when the cart opens shows a cart line&#39;s part has 0 stock, then the cart shall remove that line and give the message &quot;&lt;part name&gt; is now out of stock&quot;.</li><li><b>REQ-43</b> If the request to the parts API for current prices fails with a network or server error when the cart opens, then the cart shall show the cart lines without unit prices, line totals or totals, show an error message with a &quot;Try again&quot; button, and hide checkout until current prices load.</li></ul></details>
