<details class="serves"><summary>Serves 12 requirements</summary><ul><li><b>REQ-1</b> The portal shall provide exactly three screens for the signed-in buyer: Find parts at /parts, Cart and checkout at /cart, and My orders at /orders with the order detail panel on the same page.</li><li><b>REQ-27</b> The orders API shall return to a buyer only the orders placed by that buyer.</li><li><b>REQ-28</b> When a buyer requests their orders, the orders API shall return them newest first, each with order number, date placed, number of items (total of all quantities), total and status.</li><li><b>REQ-29</b> When the buyer picks a status filter on My orders, the orders API shall return only that buyer&#39;s orders with that status.</li><li><b>REQ-30</b> When a buyer opens one of their orders, the orders API shall return its lines (part number, name, quantity, unit price), delivery address, delivery option, total and status.</li><li><b>REQ-31</b> When the buyer opens an order, the portal shall show a status timeline Placed → Packed → Dispatched → Delivered with the current status marked by text as well as colour.</li><li><b>REQ-32</b> While an order&#39;s status is Placed, the portal shall show a &quot;Cancel order&quot; button in the order detail that asks for confirmation before calling the cancel API.</li><li><b>REQ-33</b> When a buyer cancels their order whose status is still Placed, the orders API shall set the status to Cancelled.</li><li><b>REQ-34</b> If the order&#39;s status is no longer Placed when the buyer confirms cancelling, then the orders API shall refuse with status 409 and leave the status unchanged.</li><li><b>REQ-35</b> While the buyer has no orders, the portal shall show &quot;No orders yet&quot; and a link to Find parts on My orders.</li><li><b>REQ-36</b> The portal shall show all three screens without horizontal scrolling at viewport widths from 360 px upwards.</li><li><b>REQ-37</b> The portal shall give every form field a visible text label and let the buyer reach and use every control by keyboard alone.</li></ul></details>
